Year 2,6-7,Autumn,,Place value,7.0,7,123,Flexibly partition numbers to 100,Flexibly partition numbers to 100,"So far, children have only partitioned numbers in a standard way. In this small step, they are introduced to the idea of flexible partitioning. The use of straws or other familiar representations can support children with this. If children know that 27 is made up of 2 bundles of 10 straws and 7 more straws, then by physically unbundling 1 group of 10 straws they see that 27 could also be made up of 1 bundle of 10 straws and 17 more straws. While there are numerous ways to partition numbers flexibly, the focus here is on “unbundling” 10s rather than more unusual partitions. This knowledge will prove essential later in the year when looking at calculations that cross a ten boundary and is also fundamental to later learning in higher key stages.","So far, children have only partitioned numbers in a standard way. In this small step, they are introduced to the idea of flexible partitioning. The use of straws or other familiar representations can support children with this. If children know that 27 is made up of 2 bundles of 10 straws and 7 more straws, then by physically unbundling 1 group of 10 straws they see that 27 could also be made up of 1 bundle of 10 straws and 17 more straws. While there are numerous ways to partition numbers flexibly, the focus here is on “unbundling” 10s rather than more unusual partitions. This knowledge will prove essential later in the year when looking at calculations that cross a ten boundary and is also fundamental to later learning in higher key stages.","So far, children have only partitioned numbers in a standard way. In this small step, they are introduced to the idea of flexible partitioning. The use of straws or other familiar representations can support children with this. If children know that 27 is made up of 2 bundles of 10 straws and 7 more straws, then by physically unbundling 1 group of 10 straws they see that 27 cou