Year 3,7-8,Autumn,,Addition and subtraction,19.0,19,272,Complements to 100,Complements to 100,"focus on fluently finding complements to 100 Previously in this block and in Year 2, children covered number bonds for ones to 10 and tens to 100, and this understanding can support finding complements to 100 A common misconception when finding a complement to 100 is to think that the ones digits bond to 10 and the tens digits bond to 100, which leads to a total of 110 rather than 100, for example 36 + 74. Using a hundred square can help children to avoid this misconception and to identify that they actually need to find a bond to 10 and a bond to 90. A number line can also support the development of efficient mental strategies to find complements to 100 This small step provides a good opportunity to recap prior learning on money, specifically the fact that there are 100p in £1 Complements to 100 Year 3 | Autumn term | Block 2 – Addition and subtraction | Step 19","focus on fluently finding complements to 100 Previously in this block and in Year 2, children covered number bonds for ones to 10 and tens to 100, and this understanding can support finding complements to 100 A common misconception when finding a complement to 100 is to think that the ones digits bond to 10 and the tens digits bond to 100, which leads to a total of 110 rather than 100, for example 36 + 74. Using a hundred square can help children to avoid this misconception and to identify that they actually need to find a bond to 10 and a bond to 90. A number line can also support the development of efficient mental strategies to find complements to 100 This small step provides a good opportunity to recap prior learning on money, specifically the fact that there are 100p in £1 Complements to 100 Year 3 | Autumn term | Block 2 – Addition and subtraction | Step 19","focus on fluently finding complements to 100 Previously in this block and in Year 2, children covered number bonds for ones to 10 and tens to 100, an