Year 3,7-8,Autumn,,Multiplication and division A,3.0,3,277,Multiples of 2,Multiples of 2,"In Year 2, children explored the link between counting in 2s and the 2 times-table. This small step provides the opportunity to revisit and consolidate this learning while focusing on multiples of 2 Children should be able to identify whether or not a number is a multiple of 2. They should understand that, by definition, multiples of 2 are numbers that can be divided into two equal groups. Children use their knowledge of multiples of 2 to decide if a number is even or odd. They learn to recognise that a whole number is even if it has an even number of ones, regardless of whether the tens and hundreds digits are odd. For example, 576 is even because there are 6 ones and 6 is even.","In Year 2, children explored the link between counting in 2s and the 2 times-table. This small step provides the opportunity to revisit and consolidate this learning while focusing on multiples of 2 Children should be able to identify whether or not a number is a multiple of 2. They should understand that, by definition, multiples of 2 are numbers that can be divided into two equal groups. Children use their knowledge of multiples of 2 to decide if a number is even or odd. They learn to recognise that a whole number is even if it has an even number of ones, regardless of whether the tens and hundreds digits are odd. For example, 576 is even because there are 6 ones and 6 is even.","In Year 2, children explored the link between counting in 2s and the 2 times-table. This small step provides the opportunity to revisit and consolidate this learning while focusing on multiples of 2 Children should be able to identify whether or not a number is a multiple of 2. They should understand that, by definition, multiples of 2 are numbers that can be divided into two equal groups. Children use their knowledge of multiples of 2 to decide if a number is even or odd. They learn to recognise that a whole number is eve