Year 7,11-12,Spring,,Fractions and percentages of amounts,4.0,4,842,Percentage of an amount (calculator),Percentage of an amount (calculator),"In this small step, students use a calculator to find a percentage of an amount. It is unlikely that students will have used a calculator to find percentages before, and this is a good opportunity to explore the variety of methods available. Students may initially use methods from the previous step, so ensure that they work with percentages such as 83% to help highlight the efficiency of using a calculator. One approach is to work out 1% of an amount by dividing by 100, then multiply by the required percentage. Alternative methods include using a decimal or fractional equivalent or the percentage button on the calculator. If necessary, limit the number of methods to avoid potential confusion. Students will formally begin to use a decimal multiplier to find percentages in Year 8 This step provides the opportunity to discuss percentage problems in context, such as interest rates and commission charges.","In this small step, students use a calculator to find a percentage of an amount. It is unlikely that students will have used a calculator to find percentages before, and this is a good opportunity to explore the variety of methods available. Students may initially use methods from the previous step, so ensure that they work with percentages such as 83% to help highlight the efficiency of using a calculator. One approach is to work out 1% of an amount by dividing by 100, then multiply by the required percentage. Alternative methods include using a decimal or fractional equivalent or the percentage button on the calculator. If necessary, limit the number of methods to avoid potential confusion. Students will formally begin to use a decimal multiplier to find percentages in Year 8 This step provides the opportunity to discuss percentage problems in context, such as interest rates and commission charges.","In this small step, stude