Year 8,12-13,Autumn,,Algebraic manipulation,2.0,2,914,"Identify and use formulae, expressions, identities and equations","Identify and use formulae, expressions, identities and equations","In this small step, students cement their understanding of expressions, equations, formulae and identities, before using them in context. Students were introduced to expressions and equations in Year 7 and will have experience of working with formulae in previous blocks such as area, but this is the first time that they explicitly compare and distinguish them. It is important that students know that an identity is true for any value of the variable(s) and includes the symbol æ, whereas an equation is equal only for specific values. A formula differs from an equation as it can be used to find the value of a specific variable, given the value of other variables within the formula. It is worth noting that a formula can be used to generate an equation that can then be solved.","In this small step, students cement their understanding of expressions, equations, formulae and identities, before using them in context. Students were introduced to expressions and equations in Year 7 and will have experience of working with formulae in previous blocks such as area, but this is the first time that they explicitly compare and distinguish them. It is important that students know that an identity is true for any value of the variable(s) and includes the symbol æ, whereas an equation is equal only for specific values. A formula differs from an equation as it can be used to find the value of a specific variable, given the value of other variables within the formula. It is worth noting that a formula can be used to generate an equation that can then be solved.","In this small step, students cement their understanding of expressions, equations, formulae and identities, before using them in context. Students were introduced to expressions and equations in Year 7 and will have experience of working wit