Year 8,12-13,Autumn,,Multiply and divide fractions,7.0,7,942,Divide fractions,Divide fractions,"In this small step, students learn to divide a proper fraction by a proper fraction, consolidating the methods taught in previous steps. It may be helpful to recap multiplying fractions and finding the reciprocal of a number. Students have learned to divide fractions by converting them to have the same denominators and then dividing the numerators, as well as rewriting the division as a multiplication by the reciprocal of the divisor. In this step, they should focus on identifying the most efficient method for dividing fractions rather than relying on mnemonics such as “KFC” (keep, flip, change). While such shortcuts may provide a quick fix, they do not help students to develop a deeper understanding of the process. Instead, they should think about when to apply the reciprocal method and how it relates to the concept of division.","In this small step, students learn to divide a proper fraction by a proper fraction, consolidating the methods taught in previous steps. It may be helpful to recap multiplying fractions and finding the reciprocal of a number. Students have learned to divide fractions by converting them to have the same denominators and then dividing the numerators, as well as rewriting the division as a multiplication by the reciprocal of the divisor. In this step, they should focus on identifying the most efficient method for dividing fractions rather than relying on mnemonics such as “KFC” (keep, flip, change). While such shortcuts may provide a quick fix, they do not help students to develop a deeper understanding of the process. Instead, they should think about when to apply the reciprocal method and how it relates to the concept of division.","In this small step, students learn to divide a proper fraction by a proper fraction, consolidating the methods taught in previous steps. It may be helpful to recap multiplying fractions and finding the reciprocal of 