Year 8,12-13,Autumn,,Multiply and divide fractions,8.0,8,943,Multiply and divide mixed numbers,Multiply and divide mixed numbers,"In this small step, students build on their understanding of using proper fractions to multiply and divide mixed numbers. Ensure that students can confidently convert between mixed numbers and improper fractions before attempting to multiply and divide them. Start by multiplying a mixed number by an integer, supporting students by linking multiplication with repeated addition. As their confidence grows, explore multiplying and then dividing mixed numbers. Bar models or circles can illustrate division using the grouping definition, for example how many 2 3 go into 2 2 3 . Remind students that finding the reciprocal of a mixed number is easier when it is written as an improper fraction. If appropriate, students could explore cross-simplifying fractions before multiplying to simplify calculations.","In this small step, students build on their understanding of using proper fractions to multiply and divide mixed numbers. Ensure that students can confidently convert between mixed numbers and improper fractions before attempting to multiply and divide them. Start by multiplying a mixed number by an integer, supporting students by linking multiplication with repeated addition. As their confidence grows, explore multiplying and then dividing mixed numbers. Bar models or circles can illustrate division using the grouping definition, for example how many 2 3 go into 2 2 3 . Remind students that finding the reciprocal of a mixed number is easier when it is written as an improper fraction. If appropriate, students could explore cross-simplifying fractions before multiplying to simplify calculations.","In this small step, students build on their understanding of using proper fractions to multiply and divide mixed numbers. Ensure that students can confidently convert between mixed numbers and improper fractions before attempting to multiply and divide t