Year 8,12-13,Autumn,,Symmetry and reflection,3.0,3,947,Reflect a shape in a horizontal or vertical line,Reflect a shape in a horizontal or vertical line,"In this small step, students make links with line symmetry to reflect shapes in a horizontal or vertical line. Start with shapes that lie on the mirror line, encouraging students to notice that this produces a new shape where the mirror line is a line of symmetry. Refer to the original shape as the “object” and the reflected shape as the “image”. Model how to reflect a shape that is not on the mirror line by counting the vertical/horizontal distance from the mirror line to the vertex of the given shape and plotting a point the same distance on the other side of the mirror line. Ensure students can reflect shapes on a coordinate grid in the x- or y-axis before reflecting shapes that cross the mirror line. Students could use tracing paper or a mirror to check their answers.","In this small step, students make links with line symmetry to reflect shapes in a horizontal or vertical line. Start with shapes that lie on the mirror line, encouraging students to notice that this produces a new shape where the mirror line is a line of symmetry. Refer to the original shape as the “object” and the reflected shape as the “image”. Model how to reflect a shape that is not on the mirror line by counting the vertical/horizontal distance from the mirror line to the vertex of the given shape and plotting a point the same distance on the other side of the mirror line. Ensure students can reflect shapes on a coordinate grid in the x- or y-axis before reflecting shapes that cross the mirror line. Students could use tracing paper or a mirror to check their answers.","In this small step, students make links with line symmetry to reflect shapes in a horizontal or vertical line. Start with shapes that lie on the mirror line, encouraging students to notice that this produces a new shape where the mirror line is a line of symmetry. Refer to th