Year 9,13-14,Autumn,,Properties of number,1.0,1,1043,"Factors, multiples and primes","Factors, multiples and primes","In this small step, students develop their understanding of identifying and distinguishing between factors, multiples and primes, building on learning from previous years. Encourage systematic listing strategies, identifying factor pairs to ensure that students list all the factors of a given number. Include square numbers, so that students are aware that the numbers in a factor pair may not always be different. Ensure that they understand the key differences between factors and multiples, linking multiples to times-table facts. They can find factors of a given number to decide whether the number is prime or not. Counters and bar models are useful representations to develop understanding of the key concepts.","In this small step, students develop their understanding of identifying and distinguishing between factors, multiples and primes, building on learning from previous years. Encourage systematic listing strategies, identifying factor pairs to ensure that students list all the factors of a given number. Include square numbers, so that students are aware that the numbers in a factor pair may not always be different. Ensure that they understand the key differences between factors and multiples, linking multiples to times-table facts. They can find factors of a given number to decide whether the number is prime or not. Counters and bar models are useful representations to develop understanding of the key concepts.","In this small step, students develop their understanding of identifying and distinguishing between factors, multiples and primes, building on learning from previous years. Encourage systematic listing strategies, identifying factor pairs to ensure that students list all the factors of a given number. Include square numbers, so that students are aware that the numbers in a factor pair may not always be different. Ensure that they understan