Year 10,14-15,Autumn,Foundation,Ratio and scale,7.0,7,1254,Ratios and scales,Ratios and scales,"In this small step, students make links between scales on a map or diagram and ratios. Ensure that students are confident with metric conversions such as converting centimetres to metres. Emphasise how scales must involve the same units when represented in a ratio. For example, if 1 cm represents 3 m, this cannot be represented using the ratio 1 : 3 because two different units are used. Provide students with strategies to convert centimetres to kilometres, such as converting to metres first, before converting to kilometres. Students should be encouraged to interpret scale diagrams, making links between the distances on the map/plan and the actual distances they represent.","In this small step, students make links between scales on a map or diagram and ratios. Ensure that students are confident with metric conversions such as converting centimetres to metres. Emphasise how scales must involve the same units when represented in a ratio. For example, if 1 cm represents 3 m, this cannot be represented using the ratio 1 : 3 because two different units are used. Provide students with strategies to convert centimetres to kilometres, such as converting to metres first, before converting to kilometres. Students should be encouraged to interpret scale diagrams, making links between the distances on the map/plan and the actual distances they represent.","In this small step, students make links between scales on a map or diagram and ratios. Ensure that students are confident with metric conversions such as converting centimetres to metres. Emphasise how scales must involve the same units when represented in a ratio. For example, if 1 cm represents 3 m, this cannot be represented using the ratio 1 : 3 because two different units are used. Provide students with strategies to convert centimetres to kilometres, such as converting to metres first, before converting to kilometres. Students