Year 10,14-15,Spring,Foundation,Interpret and represent data,2.0,2,1352,Averages from an ungrouped frequency table,Averages from an ungrouped frequency table,"In this small step, students practise calculating the mean, median and mode from ungrouped frequency tables. Students have already covered calculating the mean from a frequency table in Year 8, but this may be their first time calculating the mode and median. Begin by helping students interpret the table, identifying the values and their frequencies. For the mean, guide them to multiply each value by its frequency, total these products and divide by the overall number of data points. When finding the mode, prompt students to identify the most frequent value. For the median, guide students to explore the cumulative frequency and find the middle value either through a cumulative frequency column or an ordered list.","In this small step, students practise calculating the mean, median and mode from ungrouped frequency tables. Students have already covered calculating the mean from a frequency table in Year 8, but this may be their first time calculating the mode and median. Begin by helping students interpret the table, identifying the values and their frequencies. For the mean, guide them to multiply each value by its frequency, total these products and divide by the overall number of data points. When finding the mode, prompt students to identify the most frequent value. For the median, guide students to explore the cumulative frequency and find the middle value either through a cumulative frequency column or an ordered list.","In this small step, students practise calculating the mean, median and mode from ungrouped frequency tables. Students have already covered calculating the mean from a frequency table in Year 8, but this may be their first time calculating the mode and median. Begin by helping students interpret the table, identifying the values and their frequencies. For the mean, guide them to multiply e