Year 11,15-16,Spring,Foundation,Constructions and Loci,5.0,5,1653,Construct a perpendicular bisector,Construct a perpendicular bisector,"In this small step, students use a pair of compasses to construct the perpendicular bisector of a line segment, a skill they may have previously encountered in Year 9. This step provides an opportunity to revisit and practise the technique before applying it to loci problems. Explain that a perpendicular bisector meets a line at a 90° angle and divides it into two equal parts. Use a visualiser to demonstrate how to construct a perpendicular bisector accurately. Emphasise that the compass width should be set to more than half the length of the line segment so that the arcs intersect. Remind students that both arcs must be drawn with the same radius to ensure the line segment is bisected precisely.","In this small step, students use a pair of compasses to construct the perpendicular bisector of a line segment, a skill they may have previously encountered in Year 9. This step provides an opportunity to revisit and practise the technique before applying it to loci problems. Explain that a perpendicular bisector meets a line at a 90° angle and divides it into two equal parts. Use a visualiser to demonstrate how to construct a perpendicular bisector accurately. Emphasise that the compass width should be set to more than half the length of the line segment so that the arcs intersect. Remind students that both arcs must be drawn with the same radius to ensure the line segment is bisected precisely.","In this small step, students use a pair of compasses to construct the perpendicular bisector of a line segment, a skill they may have previously encountered in Year 9. This step provides an opportunity to revisit and practise the technique before applying it to loci problems. Explain that a perpendicular bisector meets a line at a 90° angle and divides it into two equal parts. Use a visualiser to demonstrate how to construct a perpendicular bi