Year 11,15-16,Spring,Foundation,Transformations,4.0,4,1670,Reflection,Reflection,"In this small step, students build on their Key Stage 3 understanding of reflection, by reflecting shapes in mirror lines and accurately describing the transformation. Recap reflections in a drawn mirror line, emphasising that the object and image are congruent, and that each vertex is equidistant from the line of reflection. Once students are confident reflecting in drawn lines, introduce reflections defined by an equation. Remind students how to draw the equations of vertical, horizontal and diagonal lines such as y = x or y = –x. For diagonal reflections, model rotating the diagram 45° so that the mirror line becomes vertical or horizontal. Students should also be able to describe a reflection by identifying the line of reflection through corresponding points, finding their midpoints and stating the equation of the line.","In this small step, students build on their Key Stage 3 understanding of reflection, by reflecting shapes in mirror lines and accurately describing the transformation. Recap reflections in a drawn mirror line, emphasising that the object and image are congruent, and that each vertex is equidistant from the line of reflection. Once students are confident reflecting in drawn lines, introduce reflections defined by an equation. Remind students how to draw the equations of vertical, horizontal and diagonal lines such as y = x or y = –x. For diagonal reflections, model rotating the diagram 45° so that the mirror line becomes vertical or horizontal. Students should also be able to describe a reflection by identifying the line of reflection through corresponding points, finding their midpoints and stating the equation of the line.","In this small step, students build on their Key Stage 3 understanding of reflection, by reflecting shapes in mirror lines and accurately describing the transformation. Recap reflections in a drawn mirror line, emphasising that the object and 